 R←∆NEW args;caller;type;props;name;class;⎕TRAP
⍝ ⎕NEW for GUI objects: create an object as a child of the calling space and return a ref.
⍝ ⎕NEW objects are unnamed, but the client needs IDs, so a hidden name is generated.
⍝ Called as eNEW (top level) or obj.eNEW / obj.(eNEW …) via the cover ∆WC fixes in every object.
 ⎕TRAP←0 'S'
 caller←findCaller
 args←,⊆args                                   ⍝ ⊂'Form' or 'Form' props
 type←⊃args
 'eNEW: ClassName must be a character vector'⎕SIGNAL 11/⍨~(1=≢⍴type)∧0=10|⎕DR type
 props←1↓args
 :If 1=≢props ⋄ props←⊃props ⋄ :EndIf          ⍝ ⎕NEW's Y[2]; more items: eWC free-form
 ⍝ Valid ⎕NEW properties are (Name Value) pairs, but anything eWC accepts is allowed too.
 ⍝ A lone unenclosed pair ('Caption' 'Hi') must not be read positionally as a Caption.
 :If 2=≢props
 :AndIf (1=≢⍴⊃props)∧0=10|⎕DR⊃props
 :AndIf ⎕NULL≢class←findClass ⎕C type
 :AndIf (⊂⎕C⊃props)∊⎕C class.PropList,objProps
     props←⊂props
 :EndIf
 name←caller newObjName type
 :Trap 0 ⍝ Re-signal from the cover so errors land in the application, not inside EWC
     (name 1)∆WC(⊂type),{0=≢⍵:⍬ ⋄ ,⊆⍵}props ⍝ Type first, as eWC: positional properties may follow. 1: an eNEW object (∆WC sets its ⎕DF)
 :Else
     ⎕DMX.EM ⎕SIGNAL ⎕DMX.EN
 :EndTrap
 R←caller⍎name
